<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tej Narsingh Malla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tej Narsingh Malla was the last Malla king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lalitpur">Lalitpur</a> (Patan) in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu">Kathmandu</a> valley, raised to the throne by its nobles in the 1760s as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithvi-narayan-shah">Prithvi Narayan Shah</a> of Gorkha closed in on the valley. When Gorkha forces took Lalitpur in 1768 he fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhaktapur">Bhaktapur</a>, and he was captured when that city fell in 1769 and died in prison.</p></div>
